    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0591" n="425" xml:id="pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 337.11/412</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-10T01:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1917, 1 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 7, 6 p.m. Railroad repaired to Omaja, trains running to Las Tunas ten
                    miles west. Permanent military guard now stationed American settlement. Another
                    detachment entering district ordered to clear surrounding country of rebels or
                    robbers.</p>
                <p>Have received a letter from Omaja. People suffered theft of horses and supplies.
                    One youth reported whipped by rebels. Has been most isolated place Cuba and
                    totally unprotected account destruction railroad bridges for hundred miles east
                    and west.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
